! strap2_7030.strap -- RECONSTRUCTION of STRAP II as a 7030 program.
!
! >>> A RECONSTRUCTION.  IBM's STRAP II was a 7030 program; one page of its
! >>> code survives (CHM 102633945, decks/strap2_chm102633945.strap).  This
! >>> code is written here to C22-6729 (the STRAP II Systems Analysis Guide),
! >>> read in the ink.  docs/strap2_7030.md records every convention with
! >>> its page, or marks it CHOSEN.  The reference for its behaviour is the
! >>> host-side STRAP II, strap/strap2/. <<<
!
! STEP 1 (docs/strap2_7030.md "The order of work"): XINPUT and GETCHA.
! STEP 2 begun: GETFLD (see below).
! MAIN is not written yet.  The test's driver (tests/strap2_7030_drive.strap,
! NOT part of this reconstruction) is assembled after this deck and stands in
! for MAIN: it calls GETCHA to the end of the input and records what GETCHA
! gives.  tests/check_strap2_7030.py runs it on the model against strap2.
!
! LAYOUT: C22-6729 p.174 and Fig. 30 p.209.  SCSTRAP1 is sections 0, A0, A1
! and 1 in that order; SCSTRAP2 (A2, 2) will overlay A1 and 1; A3 holds the
! buffers.  Each section below starts with its banner.
!
! REGISTERS (p.175, both passes).  Only $7, $8 and $9 are free.  In Pass 1
! $3 is the A8 character from GETCHA, $13 belongs to INTOUT (XINPUT here, the
! input routine, CHOSEN) and $14 to GETCHA.  $15 is general linkage; GETCHA's
! own is SIC,GETCHZ (p.79).  CHOSEN: the routines without a LINKAGE paragraph
! read so far (XINPUT, GCOPN, GCNAME, GCPUT) link through memory cells,
! "SIC,cell", read back with LV,$8,cell; B,0($8), as GETCHA's does.  A
! routine the CHM page calls through $15 will take $15.
!
! CHARACTERS.  The input is IQS, COMREC code 5 (p.8); XINPUT converts each
! card to A8, STRAP II's internal code (p.175: "A8 character from GETCHA";
! strap/strap2/a8.py: the 48 set of RefMan printed p.166 in eight bits, and
! the internal false semicolon 0o35).  A8 used below: blank 0o20, quote
! (the comment character, p.79) 0o14, asterisk 0o54, semicolon 0o35.  In a
! VFL immediate an integer is the value: KI(BU,8),(8)54.  An index immediate
! (LVI) is a half-word address, so a character reaches $3 by GCPUT and an
! address with a bit part by LV from an XW.
!
! THE FAILURES.  Each halts at HALTE with a code in ERRC:
!    1 COMREC word 8's code is not 5, IQS (only IQS input is written)
!    2 a name longer than 64 characters (CHOSEN size of NAMEB; strap2 has no
!      limit)
!    9 a form GETFLD does not write yet (a tail, step 4's TAILOR)
!   10 GETFLD's work areas full: parentheses deeper than 7, more than 8
!      items in one, an item over its 2048-bit slot (CHOSEN sizes)
!  100+n STRAP II message n, until the error routine is written (p.176-178):
!      149 a symbol over 128 characters, 156 a system symbol not found
!      (MBSPEC's 129 is a note: NOTEC, NOTEL), 163 a digit too large for the
!      radix (p.71: the digit is still used; here it halts), 166 SYNTAX
!      ERROR, 167 INAPPROPRIATE CHARACTER, 168 a number over 24 bits
!
! STEP 2, sub-slice a (docs/strap2_7030.md): GETFLD (Charts BI-BK
! pp.80-82) over numbers (CPLTNM, Chart BD p.70, in floating point as Box 1
! says), programmer symbols without tails (CPLTSY, Chart BE p.72), and the
! operators + - * / . and unary minus.  REGISTERS: GETFLD's coded
! expression pointer is $2 (p.84 Box 1, p.85 Boxes 34-38: "$2 is spaced");
! p.175 gives $2 to RNX, so GETFLD saves it on entry and restores it on
! exit, as p.175 asks of any register other than $7, $8 and $9.
!
        SLC, (8)2000.0
!
! ======== SECTION 0: subroutines common to Pass 1 and Pass 2 (p.174) ===
ERROR   ST(BU,24), ERRC
HALTE   BEW, $
!
! ======== SECTION A0: common constants and work areas, the I-O work
! ======== areas, the messages (p.174) ==================================
        CNOP
ERRC    DD(BU,64), 0
! NOTEC, NOTEL: messages that are notes (not halts), counted, the last
! one's number kept, until the error routine is written (CHOSEN)
NOTEC   DD(BU,64), 0
NOTEL   DD(BU,64), 0
XINLK   DD(BU,64), 0
XTMP    DD(BU,64), 0
HAVEN   DD(BU,64), 0
GCNEXT  DRZ(BU,64), 10
! IQSA8: IQS code (strap/charsets.py IQS) to A8 (strap/strap2/a8.py), one
! byte per IQS code; a code with no A8 character is 0, as a8() gives.
! Generated from those two tables, 2026-11-12.
IQSA8   SYN, $
        DD(BU,64), (16)1000000000000000
        DD(BU,64), (16)0000000000000000
        DD(BU,64), (16)0000000000000000
        DD(BU,64), (16)0000000000000000
        DD(BU,64), (16)00302B0B2C1C113C
